1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,600
This is Press.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,720
One phone keeps score for the whole

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:10,100
group — skins, Nassau, Wolf, the lot

4
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,800
— and it does the math while

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,560
you play.

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,700
No account, no app store, nothing to

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,300
install.

8
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:21,520
Here's a full round in four minutes.

9
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:27,280
Start New Round, and type everyone in.

10
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,400
The handicap goes in the box beside

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,420
the name — that's what every net

12
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:33,960
score in the round comes off.

13
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:37,140
Press remembers your regular crew, so next

14
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,860
week this is one tap.

15
00:00:40,547 --> 00:00:41,286
Open Course.

16
00:00:41,286 --> 00:00:43,873
Search for it and Press pulls in

17
00:00:43,873 --> 00:00:46,460
the pars and the stroke indexes, or

18
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,308
load one you saved earlier.

19
00:00:48,308 --> 00:00:50,895
Either way the card opens right here

20
00:00:50,895 --> 00:00:53,112
— and search data gets read before

21
00:00:53,112 --> 00:00:55,699
you see it, so anything that looks

22
00:00:55,699 --> 00:00:56,808
off is flagged.

23
00:00:56,808 --> 00:00:59,395
Check it against the real card once,

24
00:00:59,395 --> 00:01:00,504
then save it.

25
00:01:00,504 --> 00:01:02,721
Everything downstream — every stroke anybody gets

26
00:01:02,721 --> 00:01:04,569
— comes off these eighteen numbers.

27
00:01:06,329 --> 00:01:08,189
Games is where the money starts.

28
00:01:09,429 --> 00:01:11,309
Tap what you're playing.

29
00:01:11,309 --> 00:01:14,369
Every format carries its own rules behind

30
00:01:14,369 --> 00:01:18,229
the info button — so when somebody

31
00:01:18,229 --> 00:01:20,029
at the table has never played Wolf,

32
00:01:20,029 --> 00:01:21,989
you don't have to be the one

33
00:01:21,989 --> 00:01:22,749
who explains it.

34
00:01:24,296 --> 00:01:25,336
The full list:

35
00:01:26,096 --> 00:01:29,436
stroke play, match play — singles or

36
00:01:29,436 --> 00:01:33,456
two-man best ball — skins, Stableford, Wolf,

37
00:01:33,916 --> 00:01:37,096
Vegas with the birdie flip, Quota, Nassau

38
00:01:37,096 --> 00:01:40,096
with presses, and a Thursday-night league format.

39
00:01:41,216 --> 00:01:43,216
Net runs through all of it:

40
00:01:43,916 --> 00:01:46,216
one stroke per hole down the stroke

41
00:01:46,216 --> 00:01:48,816
index, and a second on the hardest

42
00:01:48,816 --> 00:01:51,376
holes when somebody's playing off more than

43
00:01:51,376 --> 00:01:51,976
eighteen.

44
00:01:53,496 --> 00:01:55,616
Money sets the stake per game.

45
00:01:56,456 --> 00:01:58,116
Five a skin, twenty on the Nassau.

46
00:01:58,116 --> 00:02:01,336
Leave it blank and you're playing for

47
00:02:01,336 --> 00:02:03,816
nothing — and you can change it

48
00:02:03,816 --> 00:02:04,676
mid-round from the Board.

49
00:02:06,366 --> 00:02:09,546
Start Round, and this is where you

50
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:11,966
live for the next four hours.

51
00:02:13,126 --> 00:02:17,026
Hole number, par, one row per player.

52
00:02:18,146 --> 00:02:18,766
Tap the score.

53
00:02:19,946 --> 00:02:21,626
Par is the chip in the middle,

54
00:02:22,286 --> 00:02:25,006
and the dots beside a name are

55
00:02:25,006 --> 00:02:26,706
the strokes they're getting on this hole.

56
00:02:28,366 --> 00:02:30,526
The line at the top is the

57
00:02:30,526 --> 00:02:33,186
money, live, all round.

58
00:02:34,246 --> 00:02:36,246
Close out a hole and it tells

59
00:02:36,246 --> 00:02:39,266
you exactly what just changed hands, and

60
00:02:39,266 --> 00:02:40,246
who it came from.

61
00:02:41,636 --> 00:02:45,336
Greenies, sandies, barkies — claim them on

62
00:02:45,336 --> 00:02:47,116
the hole and they land on the

63
00:02:47,796 --> 00:02:49,116
card, priced.

64
00:02:49,116 --> 00:02:51,386
Wolf picks its partner right here, before

65
00:02:51,396 --> 00:02:52,196
anybody's hit.

66
00:02:53,076 --> 00:02:54,116
Nassau presses too:

67
00:02:54,856 --> 00:02:56,756
take one by hand, or set it

68
00:02:56,756 --> 00:02:58,816
to press automatically when a side goes

69
00:02:58,816 --> 00:02:59,496
two down.

70
00:03:01,116 --> 00:03:03,256
The Board tab is every game at

71
00:03:03,256 --> 00:03:05,176
once — who's up in the match,

72
00:03:05,396 --> 00:03:08,096
who's holding skins, where the money actually

73
00:03:08,096 --> 00:03:08,696
sits.

74
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:11,356
Somebody gave you the wrong handicap on

75
00:03:11,356 --> 00:03:11,956
the first tee?

76
00:03:12,576 --> 00:03:14,796
Fix it here, and every board behind

77
00:03:14,796 --> 00:03:15,936
it recalculates.

78
00:03:17,583 --> 00:03:19,963
Card is the whole scorecard, eighteen across.

79
00:03:19,963 --> 00:03:23,343
Tap a number to fix it, tap

80
00:03:23,343 --> 00:03:25,063
a hole to jump straight back to

81
00:03:25,063 --> 00:03:25,663
it.

82
00:03:26,763 --> 00:03:29,223
Finish the round and Press settles it.

83
00:03:29,223 --> 00:03:32,743
Winner up top, then the superlatives —

84
00:03:32,743 --> 00:03:36,603
Shot of the Day, The Snowman, The

85
00:03:36,603 --> 00:03:42,183
ATM, Sandbagger — and each one cites

86
00:03:42,183 --> 00:03:44,233
the number it's based on, so the

87
00:03:44,243 --> 00:03:47,843
argument is short.

88
00:03:49,723 --> 00:03:52,023
Then the bit that normally takes ten

89
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:53,163
minutes in the car park.

90
00:03:54,003 --> 00:03:56,763
Press resolves the whole group into the

91
00:03:56,763 --> 00:04:00,343
fewest payments that settle it.

92
00:04:00,343 --> 00:04:02,163
Three people pay, not twelve.

93
00:04:03,863 --> 00:04:06,223
Share gives you the scoreboard as an

94
00:04:06,223 --> 00:04:08,583
image, or the full card as an

95
00:04:08,583 --> 00:04:10,943
image — both straight into the group chat.

96
00:04:12,673 --> 00:04:14,613
And underneath, the round itself.

97
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:17,793
The whole thing is packed into the

98
00:04:17,793 --> 00:04:20,543
link — point another phone's camera at

99
00:04:20,553 --> 00:04:21,973
the code and it opens in their

100
00:04:21,973 --> 00:04:22,813
copy of Press.

101
00:04:23,773 --> 00:04:24,693
Nothing is uploaded.

102
00:04:25,753 --> 00:04:27,133
No server ever sees it.

103
00:04:30,373 --> 00:04:33,313
On their phone it arrives held —

104
00:04:33,313 --> 00:04:35,493
sent to you, not saved — until

105
00:04:35,493 --> 00:04:37,313
they tap Keep it.

106
00:04:37,713 --> 00:04:39,573
Mid-round, the same link hands the card

107
00:04:39,873 --> 00:04:41,853
over and they carry on scoring from

108
00:04:41,853 --> 00:04:43,293
where you stopped.

109
00:04:43,293 --> 00:04:45,193
And if you both end up keeping

110
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:47,873
score, Press puts the two cards side

111
00:04:47,873 --> 00:04:51,053
by side and asks which one is

112
00:04:51,053 --> 00:04:51,653
real.

113
00:04:53,053 --> 00:04:54,193
Which brings us to the thing that

114
00:04:54,193 --> 00:04:55,953
actually matters out on the course.

115
00:04:56,773 --> 00:04:57,373
Watch:

116
00:04:57,713 --> 00:04:59,173
I'm killing the network completely.

117
00:05:00,073 --> 00:05:00,673
Reload.

118
00:05:01,293 --> 00:05:02,793
Still there, still scoring.

119
00:05:03,973 --> 00:05:06,513
Every round, every saved course, every bit

120
00:05:06,513 --> 00:05:08,333
of history lives on your phone.

121
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:11,833
That's the privacy story too — there's

122
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:13,873
no account to make, and nothing to

123
00:05:13,873 --> 00:05:14,473
leak.

124
00:05:15,723 --> 00:05:17,303
Add it to your home screen and

125
00:05:17,303 --> 00:05:19,283
it opens like anything else on your

126
00:05:19,983 --> 00:05:20,113
phone.

127
00:05:20,123 --> 00:05:24,363
It's free, it's at pressgolf.netlify.app, and the

128
00:05:24,363 --> 00:05:25,103
link's in the description.

129
00:05:25,103 --> 00:05:27,343
Now go take their money.
